-unstructured">Hammerschmidt O (1934) &#x000dc;ber die Genauigkeit der haptischen Verwirklichung geometrischer Grundbegriffe. B Sporn, Zeulenroda </citation></ref><ref id="CR10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Helbig</surname><given-names>HB</given-names></name><name><surname>Ernst</surname><given-names>MO</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Optimal integration of shape information from vision and touch</article-title><source>Exp Brain Res</source><year>2007</year><volume>179</volume><fpage>595</fpage><lpage>606</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s00221-006-0814-y</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Helbig HB, Ernst MO (2007) Optimal integration of shape information from vision and touch. Exp Brain Res 179:595&#x02013;606 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17225091</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Henriques</surname><given-names>DYP</given-names></name><name><surname>Soechting</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Bias and sensitivity in the haptic perception of geometry</article-title><source>Exp Brain Res</source><year>2003</year><volume>150</volume><fpage>95</fpage><lpage>108</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Henriques DYP, Soechting JF (2003) Bias and sensitivity in the haptic perception of geometry. Exp Brain Res 150:95&#x02013;108 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12698221</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jenmalm</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Birznieks</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Goodwin</surname><given-names>AW</given-names></name><name><surname>Johansson</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Influence of object shape on responses of human tactile afferents under conditions characteristic of manipulation</article-title><source>Eur J Neurosci</source><year>2003</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>164</fpage><lpage>176</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1460-9568.2003.02721.x</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Jenmalm P, Birznieks I, Goodwin AW, Johansson RS (2003) Influence of object shape on responses of human tactile afferents under conditions characteristic of manipulation. Eur J Neurosci 18:164&#x02013;176 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12859350</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kappers</surname><given-names>AML</given-names></name><name><surname>Koenderink</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Haptic unilateral and bilateral discrimination of curved surfaces</article-title><source>Perception</source><year>1996</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>739</fpage><lpage>749</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1068/p250739</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Kappers AML, Koenderink JJ (1996) Haptic unilateral and bilateral discrimination of curved surfaces. Perception 25:739&#x02013;749 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8888305</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kappers</surname><given-names>AML</given-names></name><name><surname>Koenderink</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Te Pas</surname><given-names>SF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Haptic discrimination of doubly curved surfaces</article-title><source>Perception</source><year>1994</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>1483</fpage><lpage>1490</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1068/p231483</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Kappers AML, Koenderink JJ, Te Pas SF (1994) Haptic discrimina